-- ============================================================================
--  SECTION 13 — Known limits, stated plainly
-- ============================================================================
--
--  * service_role and the table owner bypass RLS by design. This schema does not
--    use FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, because forcing it would also restrict
--    administrative operations performed from the dashboard. Anyone holding the
--    service_role key can read and write everything; that key must never leave
--    the server.
--
--  * Read auditing is guaranteed only for the patient_read() path. Lists and
--    searches are ordinary REST selects and are not audited (see
--    docs/TEST-AND-DEPLOY.md §4). Closing that gap means routing all reads
--    through server functions.
--
--  * bootstrap_clinic() checks then inserts without a lock, so two simultaneous
--    first requests from the same new account could in principle create two
--    clinics. Low likelihood, and recoverable by an administrator.
--
--  * add_clinic_member() and remove_clinic_member() reveal whether an email
--    address has a registered account. Only owners can call them.
--
--  * Deleting a clinic cascades to its members and clinical rows. Storage
--    objects are NOT removed by that cascade — clear the bucket path separately.
--
--  * An owner can grant themselves nothing they do not already have, but an
--    owner CAN promote another member to owner. That is intended; it is the
--    escape hatch when the original owner leaves.
-- ============================================================================

