## 6. Deploying to a public HTTPS URL (directive §8)

I cannot do this for you — there is no deployment tool in this environment, and I will not invent a
URL. `site/` is a plain static folder with no build step and only relative paths, so any static host
works. Netlify is the quickest.

### 6.1 Environment configuration

There is **no build-time environment** to configure. Two values exist and both are runtime:

| Value | Where it goes | Secret? |
|---|---|---|
| Project URL | `site/config.js`, or Settings → Server backend | No |
| **Anon** key | Same | **No — public by design** |
| AI provider key | **Nowhere in this app.** A server-side proxy holds it | — |
| **service_role** key | **Never in this repository.** Server or dashboard only | **Yes** |

To publish with the backend pre-configured, copy `site/config.example.js` to `site/config.js` and
fill it in. To keep the project URL out of the bundle, skip `config.js` and have each device enter the
values in Settings instead.

### 6.2 Deploy — Netlify

1. Go to `app.netlify.com/drop`.
2. Drag the **`site`** folder — the folder itself, not its contents.
3. Wait for the upload. You get an HTTPS URL such as `https://something.netlify.app`.
4. Optional: add a custom domain in Site settings → Domain management.
5. `site/_headers` is picked up automatically and applies the security headers (CSP, `nosniff`,
   `no-referrer`, frame-deny).

Cloudflare Pages (direct upload) and GitHub Pages work the same way.

### 6.3 Verify the deployment

| Check | Expected |
|---|---|
| Open the URL | The Dashboard loads over HTTPS. Nothing is blocked by the CSP — check the browser console for zero errors. |
| Append `/index.html` | The same Dashboard — direct URL access works |
| Reload the page twice | Still the Dashboard; it does not 404 |
| Open a second browser | The app loads, with its own (empty) data |
| Open on a phone | The responsive layout engages; the menu button opens the sidebar; tapping content closes it |
| Navigate to each of the 13 modules | All load; patient-dependent ones show the selection prompt |
| Check the padlock and certificate | Valid HTTPS, no mixed-content warnings |
| Try `/tests/engine-tests.html` and `/README.md` | **404 — neither should ship.** If either loads, remove `tests/` and the documentation from the deployed folder. |

### 6.4 If you deploy with a backend

Add your deployment's origin to Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration → Site URL and redirect
URLs, or email confirmation links will point at `localhost` and fail.

