## 3. What was verified

### 3.1 Inventory — complete

| Item | Count | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Application source files | 20 | present (16 JS modules, 2 stylesheets, `index.html`, favicon) |
| Self-test page | 1 | present, **not yet executed** |
| Documentation | 4 | README, this report, database schema, backend/security |
| Deploy metadata | 2 | registry entry + apply notes |

### 3.2 Defects found by static review and fixed before delivery

Static review is weaker than execution, but it was not merely cosmetic — seven genuine defects were
found and corrected. Recording them is part of the evidence that the review had teeth.

| # | File | Defect | Impact had it shipped |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `copilot.js` | A malformed promise chain in the response assembler (`finish`/`finalise` calling each other with unused closure variables) | Every copilot response would have resolved to `undefined` |
| 2 | `app.js` | `ui` was referenced throughout but never bound to `CN.ui` | `ReferenceError` on every Copilot render and on any module-not-found path |
| 3 | `views-core.js` | The patient-row click handler also fired when **Edit** or **Delete** was clicked, because `closest()` matched the enclosing row | Clicking Delete opened the record *and* raised the delete dialog |
| 4 | `views-planning.js` | Version-diff "added" rows called a non-existent helper inside a meaningless ternary | Diff output corrupted |
| 5 | `views-planning.js` | The reassessment-apply handler referenced an undefined variable (`resultSuggestedValue`) instead of `result.suggested` | Approving a new target would have written `undefined` as the calorie target |
| 6 | `views-clinical.js` | A dead conditional in the rate tile and a no-op goal-change branch | Cosmetic, but misleading |
| 7 | `views-core.js` | Dead helper functions containing a broken value lookup | Latent trap for future edits |

Defects 1, 2 and 5 were functional blockers. Defect 3 would have caused destructive-action confusion.

### 3.3 Invariants confirmed by inspection

- **No green is reachable.** `charts.js` draws only from `navy`, `gold`, `burgundy`; the semantic
  state classes in `app.css` map to the same three. No green hex appears in any stylesheet.
- **No external references.** `index.html` contains no external URL. The only outbound links in the
  entire application are user-initiated, inert links in Clinical References, which the hosting policy
  permits.
- **Script order is correct** and each module depends only on those loaded above it.
- **Approval is structurally enforced.** `engine.assess` returns a target; the Plan Builder refuses to
  generate without an assessment carrying `approvedAt`. Reassessment returns `applied: false` and
  `requiresApproval: true` unconditionally.
- **Deficit is never derived from BMR.** `assess()` applies the deficit to `tdee.value` and clamps
  against both a sex-specific floor and a 30%-of-TDEE ceiling before returning.
- **History is append-only in code.** Plan edits mutate the active version but new versions are
  appended and old ones retained; `diff()` compares any two.

