## 3.4 Second-pass review — recovery pass

A later pass re-audited the build against the brief's 23 sections and closed the gaps that were
reachable without a server.

### Features added

| Brief | Feature |
|---|---|
| §4 | **Document attachments** — lab and body-composition files stored in the browser, listed, downloadable back, deletable. Lab report and body-composition attachment was previously an unimplemented input. |
| §4 | **Blood pressure** — recorded into the same append-only measurement history, shown on the Assessment screen and included in printed reports. |
| §3 | **Clinician-defined custom fields** — defined in Settings, rendered on every patient record, no source change. This is an explicit brief requirement that was entirely absent. |
| §18 | **Clinic reporting** — search and filter across the patient list by name, ID, phone, condition, clinical goal, registration date range and follow-up status. |
| §12 | **Custom recipes** — ingredient list, quantities, servings and finished yield, with per-ingredient, whole-recipe and per-serving nutrition computed rather than entered. |

### Defects found and fixed in this pass

| # | Defect | Impact had it shipped |
|---|---|---|
| 8 | `views-clinical.js` rendered a file input with **no handler** | A decorative control — precisely what brief §21 prohibits ("no fake buttons, non-functional modules") |
| 9 | The in-memory store cloned records with `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))` | **Silent data loss.** A `File`/`Blob` stringifies to `{}`, so an attachment write would report success while destroying the document. Replaced with a clone that carries blobs by reference. |
| 10 | Backup serialised the whole store to JSON | Attachment binaries would have become `{}` in the backup file without warning. Now the binaries are stripped deliberately and the omission is declared in the backup envelope, with metadata retained. |
| 11 | Plan items resolved their name only by live food lookup | A food renamed or removed from the database would leave unreadable entries in a stored, approved plan. Added a name snapshot at item creation plus an `itemName()` resolver that falls back to it. |
| 12 | Mistyped i18n key (`rc.persServing`) | Would have rendered as "PersServing" |

Defect 9 is the most serious of the whole project: it was silent corruption of the very feature being
added, and it would only have surfaced as unexplained missing documents.

### Storage schema change

`DB_VERSION` was raised from 1 to 2 to add the `attachments`, `recipes` and `kb` object stores. An
existing version-1 database upgrades in place: the upgrade handler creates only the stores that are
missing, so no existing records are touched or dropped.

