## 4. What could NOT be verified — and the honest caveats

| Item | Why | Remedy |
|---|---|---|
| **The application renders at all** | Browser unavailable after the first probe | Open `site/index.html` |
| **The ~90 engine assertions pass** | Needs a browser to execute | Open `tests/engine-tests.html` — this is the single most important next step |
| Module syntax validity | No shell, so no `node --check` | Command is in the README |
| Plan generation quality on real data | Never executed | Generate a plan in the UI |
| Arabic shaping and RTL mirroring | Never rendered | Toggle EN ⇄ AR |
| Print/PDF pagination | Never printed | Use the report preview |
| Clinical accuracy of the food table and briefs | Authored, not transcribed from the supplied PDFs | Replace with clinic material; the PDFs remain the intended source of truth |
| The server build (brief §§19, 21) | Out of scope by decision | Designed only — see `docs/database-schema.sql` |

### Caveats that must travel with this build

1. **The clinical content is a synthesis.** The food composition values, the 20 approaches and the
   clinical briefs were written from established nutrition science and standard reference values. They
   are internally consistent and clinically plausible. They are **not** a transcription of the
   clinic's uploaded lecture material, which could not be read. Every value lives in three `data-*.js`
   files so replacement is mechanical.
2. **References are honestly marked unverified.** The briefs cite each organisation's canonical entry
   page with `verified: false` and **no access date**, and the interface labels them *not verified*.
   This is deliberate: asserting an access date for a page never opened would be a fabricated citation.
3. **The test suite has never run.** It is delivered as the verification instrument, not as evidence of
   a passing result. Passing it is the user's first action.
4. **No authentication, no audit, no encryption at rest.** Records live in the browser. Not suitable
   for real patient data until the server path in `docs/backend-and-security.md` is built.
5. **Page numbering in reports** is provided by the browser's print dialog, not by the stylesheet,
   because CSS `@page` margin boxes are not reliably supported.

