## Development quick start

No build step, no dependencies, no install.

```bash
# From this folder — recommended, so IndexedDB works
python -m http.server 8617 --bind 127.0.0.1
# then open http://127.0.0.1:8617/
```

Opening `index.html` directly via `file://` also works. Storage picks the best tier available:
**IndexedDB → localStorage → in-memory**. On `file://`, IndexedDB is typically blocked, so the app uses
localStorage and records **do** survive a reload; only the last tier is session-only, and Settings
states plainly which engine is active.

On first run you get a short clinic-identity setup, then an empty dashboard. Settings → *Load
demonstration data* adds three fictitious patients with measurements, labs, a plan and follow-ups.

