## The calculation engine is the spine

Every clinical number in the interface comes from `engine.js` or `planner.js`. Both are pure
functions — same input, same output, no I/O — which is what makes them testable and reproducible.

- **BMR** — Mifflin-St Jeor, Harris-Benedict (1919 and Roza 1984), plus device-reported and manual
  entry. A measured value is labelled as measured and never presented as an estimate.
- **TDEE** — activity factor applied to BMR, with the factor always displayed.
- **Target** — the deficit is applied to **TDEE, never to BMR**. A hard safety floor (1200 kcal
  female / 1500 kcal male) and a 30%-of-TDEE cap are enforced before any figure is shown.
- **Safety screen** — pregnancy, eating-disorder history, renal disease, type 1 diabetes, BMI under
  18.5 with a weight-loss goal, refeeding risk, and predicted loss above 1% of body weight per week
  all raise flags. Any `alert` sets *requires review*.
- **Reassessment** — proposes a revised target at follow-up and **never reduces calories for a short
  plateau alone**. Poor adherence, fluid shifts, medication changes and sub-three-week plateaus all
  hold the target steady. Every change requires clinician approval.
- **Approval is enforced** — a calorie target is stored with its approver; the Plan Builder refuses to
  generate anything without an approved target.

