## External integrations still requiring configuration

Nothing below is simulated. Each entry states what exists today and what a deployment must supply.

| Integration | Status in this build | What a deployment must provide |
|---|---|---|
| **External language model** | Proxy adapter wired (`js/copilot.js` → `callExternal`). Disabled by default; every response says whether a model was consulted. Sends **no credential**. | A server-side proxy URL in Settings. The proxy holds the API key and forwards a de-identified payload. Required contract: `POST` JSON `{instruction, patient, targets, followUpCount}` → `{text}`. |
| **Knowledge-base indexing for PDF / Word / Excel** | Formats recognised; files stored for reference; text explicitly not read and not searchable. | A server exposing `POST {base}/documents` (multipart → `{id,title,chunks}`), `GET {base}/search?q=` and `DELETE {base}/documents/{id}`. Set the base URL via `CN.kb.remote.setEndpoint()`. |
| **Live internet research** | Not implemented, and the interface says so. No claim of a search is ever made. | A search API reached through the same server-side proxy pattern, with source attribution returned alongside results. |
| **Clinical data backend** | None. Records live in the browser. | The full server build per brief §§19/21 — schema in `docs/database-schema.sql`, contract in `docs/backend-and-security.md`. |
| **PDF rendering** | Browser print-to-PDF. No external renderer. | Nothing, unless server-side PDF generation with embedded Arabic fonts is required — then a rendering service. |

**No credential belongs in this application.** `Settings → AI configuration` deliberately has no API
key field: in a browser-only build any key would be readable by whoever opens the page. That is why
the adapter is a proxy contract rather than a direct provider call.

